    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4290ad7_f5954953",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/UpdateEngineStable.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-04T02:07:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See https://source.android.com/docs/core/architecture/aidl/stable-aidl#querying-the-interface-version-of-the-remote-object\n\n\u003e For Java language, the remote side MUST implement getInterfaceVersion() and getInterfaceHash() as follows (super is used instead of IFoo to avoid copy/paste mistakes. The annotation @SuppressWarnings(\"static\") may be needed to disable warnings, depending on the javac configuration):\n\n```\nclass MyFoo extends IFoo.Stub {\n    @Override\n    public final int getInterfaceVersion() { return super.VERSION; }\n\n    @Override\n    public final String getInterfaceHash() { return super.HASH; }\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "a2d3c1b3_a98b6cdd",
